es no rollback/back-out path or opt-in guard for the new unscoped direct-GET behavior.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9f890429873f2503","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Gap; Proposed work","norm_id":"na7dc6289fb435350","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The generalized overlay causes unexpected GET-volume or latency regression on production unscoped passes and operators need to disable it quickly"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the failure-disposition contract for the ambiguous-key lag-free GET: what surfaces (retryable vs skip-key-and-defer vs preserve-local) when get_issue_by_rest fails/times out on an unscoped pass, ensuring a GET failure does NOT silently fall back to the stale snapshot value and re-open the clobber window.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract","T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6487,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan adds a new failure point: 'Direct-GET those keys, merge the mirrored scalar fields into curr_snapshot'","No AC or body text states what disposition surfaces if get_issue_by_rest fails on an unscoped pass; the fallback-to-stale-snapshot leg would silently re-open the clobber window this plan closes"],"finding":"The plan adds a lag-free direct-GET arm (get_issue_by_rest) for ambiguous keys that runs before differs and baseline advance, but never states the disposition when that GET itself fails or times out — whether the pass falls back to the stale snapshot value (re-opening the very clobber window being closed), skips arbitration for that key, or surfaces retryable.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa4ccb460dab47dba","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Proposed work: 'Direct-GET those keys, merge the mirrored scalar fields into curr_snapshot, then arbitrate on the lag-free value.'","norm_id":"ne485101c1e589a9d","priority":0.2513,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a 'Failure-disposition contract' line: on GET failure, do NOT mirror the stale snapshot for that key — preserve local (skip advancing baseline for the key) and surface the GET error as retryable so a later pass re-arbitrates.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the ambiguous-key screen reuses the existing shape-tolerant arbitration seams (outbound_fields._local_matches_prev for local==baseline and _jira_matches_prev for remote==baseline over _INBOUND_MIRRORED_FIELDS) rather than raw == / !=, so assignee/description shape differences do not mis-classify keys.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4325,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'keys where the search snapshot presents local==baseline AND snapshot-remote!=baseline'","peer_state.set_baseline normalizes via normalize_baseline_value into _BASELINE_FIELDS (vendor shape); local tickets are local shape","outbound_fields._local_matches_prev / _jira_matches_prev already implement the exact shape-tolerant local-vs-baseline and jira-vs-baseline comparisons (assignee dict-vs-string, description rstrip)","inbound_differ._diff_jira_vs_local applies ADF-fit / soft-wrap normalization before deciding description equality"],"finding":"The 'local==baseline AND remote!=baseline' ambiguity screen is specified as bare equality, but baseline is stored in vendor-normalized shape while local is local shape, and the fields involved (assignee, description) need shape-tolerant comparison. A raw == will mis-classify.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f36f64d5a2df40513","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Proposed work / AC line 1","norm_id":"nc5550c28b5ac8897","priority":0.1675,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An assignee stored locally as an email string but as a {accountId,...} dict in the baseline is judged local!=baseline and the ambiguous key is skipped, so the stale-clobber window it was meant to close stays open","A description differing only by trailing whitespace / ADF re-encoding is judged remote!=baseline spuriously, refreshing a non-ambiguous key and inflating GET volume beyond the bound the AC promises"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Define an ambiguous key as any binding+field where _local_matches_prev(field, local_val, baseline) is True AND _jira_matches_prev(field, snapshot_remote, baseline) is False, computed with the same normalization/mappers the differs use; GET only those keys.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State where the ambiguity screen obtains the per-binding LOCAL field values at the refresh site (e.g. confirm ctx exposes local_tickets_by_id or add it), since local==baseline cannot be evaluated from curr_snapshot + baseline alone.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["snapshot_lagfree_refresh.refresh_scoped_snapshot reads ctx.selection_ids, ctx.r